  // Third statement: both voices tremolo, an octave apart, which is as far
  // as this scoring goes. The melody is where it always was - the octave is
  // the original's, not ours - but nothing is held any more, and with the
  // kick and the crash under it the pair sit on the beat rather than behind
  // it. The accents are on the peaks only; a tremolo already supplies the
  // motion a swell would otherwise have to write.
  lead.upper dyn:mf..f art:tremolo feel:loose pocket:on
    | g5:4!^ | f5:4_ | g5:4^ | f5:4_ |
    | e5:4_ | f5:4_ | g5:4^ | e5:4. |
    | a5:4!^ | f5:4_ | g5:4^ | a5:4!^ |
    | g5:4_ | f5:4_ | e5:4. | g5:4^ |
  lower dyn:mf..f art:tremolo feel:loose pocket:on
    | e4:4!^ | d4:4_ | e4:4_ | d4:4_ |
    | c4:4_ | d4:4_ | e4:4^ | c4:4. |
    | f4:4!^ | d4:4_ | e4:4_ | f4:4^ |
    | e4:4_ | d4:4_ | c4:4. | e4:4^ |
